From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: mdt_loader: pass QSDK split-image metadata unchanged

QSDK-built split images, such as the IPQ5332 Q6 firmware q6_fw0/q6_fw1,
keep the hash segment at its own file offset at the end of the .mdt file.
qcom_mdt_read_metadata() repacks the hash segment directly after the ELF
headers, and TrustZone then rejects the metadata (PAS init_image returns
an invalid argument), so the Q6 cannot be authenticated.

When the hash segment ends the .mdt and does not follow the headers, pass
the .mdt to TrustZone unchanged.

Follows the fix for the same symptom in perceival/openwrt-flint3#93.

Signed-off-by: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/mdt_loader.c
@@ -197,6 +197,21 @@
 	ehdr_size = phdrs[0].p_filesz;
 	hash_size = phdrs[hash_segment].p_filesz;
 
+	/*
+	 * QSDK-style split images (e.g. IPQ5332 Q6 q6_fw0/q6_fw1) keep the
+	 * hash segment at its own p_offset and end the .mdt file with it.
+	 * TrustZone validates the metadata against those offsets, so pass
+	 * the .mdt unchanged instead of repacking the hash after the header.
+	 */
+	if (ehdr_size + hash_size != fw->size &&
+	    phdrs[hash_segment].p_offset + hash_size == fw->size) {
+		data = kmemdup(fw->data, fw->size, GFP_KERNEL);
+		if (!data)
+			return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
+		*data_len = fw->size;
+		return data;
+	}
+
 	data = kmalloc(ehdr_size + hash_size, GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!data)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
